1
00:00:31,220 --> 00:00:34,020
Let's go.

2
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:06,617
I'll

3
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:08,017
see

4
00:01:08,100 --> 00:01:13,757
you

5
00:01:13,840 --> 00:01:20,840
next

6
00:01:22,760 --> 00:01:23,590
time.

7
00:01:53,440 --> 00:01:55,257
She was actually an ultimate Digimon.

8
00:01:55,340 --> 00:01:58,077
With the help of Paildramon,
we managed to capture her,

9
00:01:58,160 --> 00:02:01,042
but Mumimum put the wraps
on us and they escaped.

10
00:02:10,140 --> 00:02:12,200
Those Digibrats made me so tense.

11
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:13,697
I've got to try to relax.

12
00:02:13,780 --> 00:02:15,477
Maybe I should think happy thoughts.

13
00:02:15,560 --> 00:02:19,420
Let's see, evil spells, crushing
my enemies, more control spires,

14
00:02:19,700 --> 00:02:20,797
less Digidestined.

15
00:02:20,880 --> 00:02:23,409
Oh, I can't keep those
kids out of my head!

16
00:02:23,540 --> 00:02:25,317
How hard can it be to get rid of them?

17
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:26,680
Where did I go wrong?

18
00:02:34,780 --> 00:02:36,220
Oh, there you are.

19
00:02:38,780 --> 00:02:42,200
Usually a bubble bath relaxes
me, but not this time.

20
00:02:44,920 --> 00:02:48,540
Arukenima, a rather unusual
place for a tub, don't you think?

21
00:02:49,180 --> 00:02:53,533
Well, I guess all you have to do is
build the rest of the house around it.

22
00:02:54,660 --> 00:02:56,520
Let's do it! Let's go get him!

23
00:02:58,960 --> 00:02:59,920
You're next!

24
00:03:00,620 --> 00:03:01,679
Desperado Blaster!

25
00:03:04,580 --> 00:03:05,410
Hello?

26
00:03:06,480 --> 00:03:08,362
That sure does look comfortable.

27
00:03:10,120 --> 00:03:12,700
I haven't had a bath like that in years.

28
00:03:13,500 --> 00:03:15,600
Do you think that I could...

29
00:03:16,460 --> 00:03:17,780
Would you be quiet?

30
00:03:18,020 --> 00:03:20,373
Can't you see I'm trying to concentrate?

31
00:03:29,920 --> 00:03:33,155
Those kids are destroying my
supply of control, Spires.

32
00:03:34,640 --> 00:03:36,405
I'll just have to work faster.

33
00:03:38,140 --> 00:03:40,357
In the meantime, mind if I take a dip?

34
00:03:40,440 --> 00:03:41,300
Fire rocket!

35
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:47,460
Way to go!

36
00:03:47,840 --> 00:03:48,860
Double star!

37
00:03:51,940 --> 00:03:52,900
Awesome!

38
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:54,420
Rock cracking!

39
00:03:59,780 --> 00:04:02,500
Digmon, nice job! Shooting star!

40
00:04:05,820 --> 00:04:07,300
That a boy!

41
00:04:07,860 --> 00:04:09,220
Rosetta, star!

42
00:04:12,760 --> 00:04:14,497
Say cheese, please!

43
00:04:14,580 --> 00:04:21,080
I can't believe it.

44
00:04:21,220 --> 00:04:23,140
We're actually making progress.

45
00:04:23,560 --> 00:04:25,700
That's 147 so far today.

46
00:04:26,100 --> 00:04:28,060
I think we could all use a break.

47
00:04:33,880 --> 00:04:35,160
Thirsty! Yeah!

48
00:04:36,300 --> 00:04:37,880
Hmm? I'm thirsty.

49
00:04:38,800 --> 00:04:39,720
Me too.

50
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:43,706
There was a vending machine with
juice in it back there a ways.

51
00:04:44,580 --> 00:04:46,440
Well, then why are we here?

52
00:04:46,680 --> 00:04:48,957
Hopefully it has milk,
preferably in a saucer.

53
00:04:49,040 --> 00:04:49,880
Count me in.

54
00:04:50,140 --> 00:04:51,500
Me too, I'm coming.

55
00:04:52,200 --> 00:04:55,517
Don't worry, we'll just get something
and bring it back to you, okay?

56
00:04:55,600 --> 00:04:56,430
Huh?

57
00:04:57,280 --> 00:04:58,110
Aw.

58
00:04:58,860 --> 00:04:59,690
Hmm.

59
00:04:59,960 --> 00:05:02,240
Hey, what kind should we get you?

60
00:05:04,400 --> 00:05:05,230
Whatever.

61
00:05:07,280 --> 00:05:09,280
Davis, what's the matter with you?

62
00:05:10,260 --> 00:05:11,090
Nothing.

63
00:05:11,460 --> 00:05:15,720
I know when something's wrong and
something's wrong. Now, what's wrong?

64
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:17,647
Stop asking me what's wrong.

65
00:05:17,800 --> 00:05:18,630
Huh?

66
00:05:18,713 --> 00:05:20,120
Hey, Davis, what's wrong?

67
00:05:20,340 --> 00:05:23,140
Uh-huh. Hmm. Hi, Oli.

68
00:05:24,060 --> 00:05:26,997
Are you just gonna stay up
there and be crabby all day?

69
00:05:27,080 --> 00:05:28,377
Look, I'm not crabby.

70
00:05:28,460 --> 00:05:30,284
Get it through your thick head.

71
00:05:30,440 --> 00:05:32,260
Ah, now there's the old Davis.

72
00:05:32,520 --> 00:05:34,537
Why don't you come down
here and we'll talk?

73
00:05:34,620 --> 00:05:35,450
Huh?

74
00:05:35,980 --> 00:05:37,720
It's about Cody and Ken.

75
00:05:38,040 --> 00:05:39,857
Have you noticed they
never talk to each other?

76
00:05:39,940 --> 00:05:43,597
They're not friends and it's not
like they argue the way you and I do.

77
00:05:43,680 --> 00:05:45,060
They just don't talk

78
00:05:46,020 --> 00:05:47,138
Yeah, you're right.

79
00:05:47,300 --> 00:05:50,837
I guess they're still both a little
nervous around each other well

80
00:05:50,920 --> 00:05:53,097
They can't go on like this much longer.

81
00:05:53,180 --> 00:05:55,357
Well, what are we supposed to do about it?

82
00:05:55,440 --> 00:05:56,270
Actually?

83
00:05:56,353 --> 00:05:57,300
I've got a plan

84
00:06:00,560 --> 00:06:01,820
It's worth a shot

85
00:06:03,540 --> 00:06:06,660
Hey, Ken Cody, I need a hand, huh?

86
00:06:08,740 --> 00:06:10,960
See that control spire over there?

87
00:06:11,560 --> 00:06:12,980
It's right behind you.

88
00:06:13,340 --> 00:06:17,458
It seems that Flamedermon wasn't
strong enough to knock that one down.

89
00:06:17,720 --> 00:06:18,760
Are you nuts?

90
00:06:18,920 --> 00:06:20,449
I can do that blindfolded.

91
00:06:21,120 --> 00:06:24,017
Quiet, it's a plan to get
Cody and Ken to work together.

92
00:06:24,100 --> 00:06:25,420
Oh, never mind.

93
00:06:29,520 --> 00:06:31,167
It's really kind of strange.

94
00:06:31,980 --> 00:06:33,560
Yeah, go figure, you know?

95
00:06:46,560 --> 00:06:52,020
Spiking Strike Lady Rock Cracking

96
00:07:03,340 --> 00:07:05,820
Yay, we did it

97
00:07:09,800 --> 00:07:13,447
Morimont and Armadillamont seem
to be getting along just fine.

98
00:07:16,540 --> 00:07:19,716
Yeah, now if only Cody and
Ken would act the same way.

99
00:07:24,900 --> 00:07:25,760
That's enough!

100
00:07:25,980 --> 00:07:28,497
You two just worked together
to destroy a control spire.

101
00:07:28,580 --> 00:07:30,357
Why don't you shake hands and be friends?

102
00:07:30,440 --> 00:07:31,270
Davis!

103
00:07:31,660 --> 00:07:32,490
What?

104
00:07:32,573 --> 00:07:35,737
I think Fladramon could have
destroyed that control spire.

105
00:07:35,820 --> 00:07:36,940
I agree with Cody.

106
00:07:37,880 --> 00:07:39,337
Well, now that you mention it...

107
00:07:39,420 --> 00:07:43,008
Davis, please don't make us
waste our energy like that again.

108
00:07:43,240 --> 00:07:45,760
Cody, you're so stubborn! Please, stop!

109
00:07:45,960 --> 00:07:47,078
You're not helping!

110
00:07:47,920 --> 00:07:51,820
It seems not every team member
wants us around, Wyrmon. Let's go.

111
00:07:54,340 --> 00:07:55,960
But wait! Kent!

112
00:07:56,300 --> 00:07:57,947
Wyrmon, where are you going?

113
00:08:00,120 --> 00:08:01,240
Ah, you!

114
00:08:03,700 --> 00:08:04,530
Cody!

115
00:08:07,120 --> 00:08:10,497
I'm going to need an
all-powerful Digimon if I ever

116
00:08:10,580 --> 00:08:13,521
hope to squeeze the life
out of the Digidestined.

117
00:08:14,600 --> 00:08:17,980
When I only used one Control Spire.

118
00:08:22,700 --> 00:08:24,660
This is what I created.

119
00:08:25,900 --> 00:08:30,080
And then I tried using ten Control Spires.

120
00:08:34,400 --> 00:08:35,640
Spirit Needle!

121
00:08:40,060 --> 00:08:43,480
And I created this powerful creature.

122
00:08:46,160 --> 00:08:50,400
And yet neither of them was sufficient
enough to defeat those kids.

123
00:08:50,920 --> 00:08:55,460
In order to destroy those kids, I'll
need to use a hundred control spires.

124
00:08:55,720 --> 00:08:59,997
If she's going to use a hundred control
spires, how many hairs does she need?

125
00:09:00,080 --> 00:09:04,433
Let's see, that's six, carry the four,
minus two, that would be a hundred.

126
00:09:04,580 --> 00:09:06,437
If you have to use a hundred hairs,

127
00:09:06,520 --> 00:09:09,520
you could get a job in the
circus as the bald lady.

128
00:09:10,520 --> 00:09:14,120
And you can join the circus
on the flying trapeze.

129
00:09:22,300 --> 00:09:28,097
Every time she treats me like that,
I feel closer and closer to her.

130
00:09:28,180 --> 00:09:30,040
Could this be love I'm feeling?

131
00:09:36,440 --> 00:09:38,077
Mummymon, would you hurry it up?

132
00:09:38,160 --> 00:09:38,990
We're leaving.

133
00:09:39,680 --> 00:09:40,600
I'm coming!

134
00:09:44,400 --> 00:09:46,777
Ninety-nine control spires
on the side of the road.

135
00:09:46,860 --> 00:09:49,437
Ninety-nine control
spires, do not one down.

136
00:09:49,520 --> 00:09:50,360
Oh, be quiet.

137
00:09:51,100 --> 00:09:53,837
Look at all those
beautiful control spires.

138
00:09:53,920 --> 00:09:58,332
I knew those eager-veaver brats didn't
have time to clean up this area yet.

139
00:10:01,020 --> 00:10:02,340
Are you ready?

140
00:10:05,300 --> 00:10:07,540
I love watching you work.

141
00:10:09,100 --> 00:10:11,340
Then you're really gonna love this.

142
00:10:11,660 --> 00:10:14,836
This creature will not only
destroy the Digidestined,

143
00:10:14,920 --> 00:10:17,280
but also the entire digital world.

144
00:10:18,480 --> 00:10:21,200
Digimon of Darkness, come to me!

145
00:10:45,640 --> 00:10:47,260
And that's the whole story.

146
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:49,245
He's been up there ever since.

147
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:53,057
We're gone ten minutes
and you cause a mutiny?

148
00:10:53,140 --> 00:10:56,997
Both of them are so stubborn, neither one
of them is willing to talk to the other.

149
00:10:57,080 --> 00:10:58,460
I feel sorry for Cody.

150
00:10:58,640 --> 00:11:00,228
I'm sure he feels terrible.

151
00:11:10,440 --> 00:11:11,740
You know what?

152
00:11:12,140 --> 00:11:13,420
I was thinking.

153
00:11:14,200 --> 00:11:17,906
Maybe I should talk to both of
them about acting their own age.

154
00:11:23,140 --> 00:11:25,140
I think I can straighten them out.

155
00:11:31,820 --> 00:11:34,180
Alright, what exactly is so funny?

156
00:11:41,220 --> 00:11:43,600
Uh, look, are you guys mad?

157
00:11:45,700 --> 00:11:48,857
You don't have to give me the
silent treatment, I mean, come on.

158
00:11:48,940 --> 00:11:51,400
Davis, take a look behind you. Huh?

159
00:11:56,780 --> 00:11:59,957
Shouldn't you boys and girls be
home with your mommies and daddies?

160
00:12:00,040 --> 00:12:01,334
None of your business!

161
00:12:01,680 --> 00:12:03,327
All right, what do you want?

162
00:12:03,860 --> 00:12:08,331
I thought you kids might enjoy playing
with a little Digimon I put together.

163
00:12:08,520 --> 00:12:09,740
When will you learn?

164
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:12,941
Every time you try to fight
us, you end up losing.

165
00:12:13,100 --> 00:12:14,380
Not this time.

166
00:12:17,400 --> 00:12:18,360
Spirit Needle!

167
00:12:33,400 --> 00:12:35,820
Have a good time. Play nice.

168
00:12:44,060 --> 00:12:44,890
Davis?

169
00:12:45,480 --> 00:12:47,100
Right. Digimon.

170
00:12:49,820 --> 00:12:50,760
Digimon!

171
00:12:54,840 --> 00:12:55,670
Digimon!

172
00:12:55,753 --> 00:12:56,583
Digimon!

173
00:12:56,666 --> 00:12:57,496
And BMON!

174
00:12:58,360 --> 00:12:59,190
Digimon!

175
00:13:01,360 --> 00:13:02,740
Digimon! Digimon!

176
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:05,900
Digimon! Digimon!

177
00:13:07,360 --> 00:13:08,360
The jump will be!

178
00:13:09,360 --> 00:13:10,190
Aramon!

179
00:13:10,273 --> 00:13:11,103
Armored Digimon! Now!

180
00:13:20,600 --> 00:13:23,300
Pegasus-man, flying home!

181
00:13:25,360 --> 00:13:26,190
Digimon!

182
00:13:27,560 --> 00:13:30,260
Pokémon Digimon 2!

183
00:13:33,240 --> 00:13:34,320
Aquilamon!

184
00:13:35,120 --> 00:13:35,950
Digimon!

185
00:13:37,320 --> 00:13:38,150
Digimon!

186
00:13:39,160 --> 00:13:41,760
Armadillo-man, Digimon 2!

187
00:13:42,260 --> 00:13:43,789
Digimon are the champions!

188
00:13:44,260 --> 00:13:45,677
Digimon, Digimon!

189
00:13:45,760 --> 00:13:47,740
Digimon Master, Ampelomon!

190
00:13:48,420 --> 00:13:49,880
Digimon Master, Digimon!

191
00:13:53,400 --> 00:13:55,400
Digi Armor, American!

192
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:57,840
Digimon, Digimon, Digimon!

193
00:13:58,540 --> 00:14:01,340
Digimon, Armor Digiball, true!

194
00:14:02,760 --> 00:14:04,054
Uncover the champions!

195
00:14:07,760 --> 00:14:09,160
Armor, Digimon!

196
00:14:10,820 --> 00:14:13,700
The Bearimon, the Angel of Light!

197
00:14:16,120 --> 00:14:17,180
Let's do it!

198
00:14:19,460 --> 00:14:20,700
Now that's funny.

199
00:14:20,940 --> 00:14:22,705
They think they have a chance.

200
00:14:28,280 --> 00:14:29,320
This is fun!

201
00:14:29,620 --> 00:14:32,149
Nothing quite relaxes
me like scaring kids.

202
00:14:32,420 --> 00:14:33,720
Come on, guys, hurry!

203
00:14:35,820 --> 00:14:37,777
I've got a bad feeling about this.

204
00:14:37,860 --> 00:14:39,625
DK and Kari are too far ahead!

205
00:14:41,800 --> 00:14:42,940
DK, what's up?

206
00:14:50,160 --> 00:14:51,900
Dory! TK!

207
00:15:03,720 --> 00:15:04,597
I...

208
00:15:04,680 --> 00:15:06,360
I know who that is.

209
00:15:08,640 --> 00:15:09,517
It's...

210
00:15:09,600 --> 00:15:11,620
it's Black War, Greymon.

211
00:15:23,340 --> 00:15:28,460
Black WarGreymon is a Mega-Digimon who
looks like WarGreymon, but he's pure evil.

212
00:15:28,800 --> 00:15:33,380
His Terra Destroyer attack releases a
concentration of 100 % negative energy.

213
00:15:33,600 --> 00:15:36,580
Black WarGreymon, it can't be.

214
00:15:37,600 --> 00:15:41,580
It is, but I don't know how it's possible.

215
00:15:42,700 --> 00:15:44,680
What should we do, Ankylomon?

216
00:15:45,280 --> 00:15:48,077
I'd say protecting the
kids is high on the list.

217
00:15:48,160 --> 00:15:49,620
I agree wholeheartedly.

218
00:16:11,620 --> 00:16:13,097
He's too strong for them.

219
00:16:13,180 --> 00:16:15,180
They need more help! Now!

220
00:16:15,460 --> 00:16:18,717
Heil Grumman is the only one
who is strong enough to help!

221
00:16:18,800 --> 00:16:19,630
That's it, then.

222
00:16:19,713 --> 00:16:20,856
We have to call Ken!

223
00:16:23,220 --> 00:16:25,044
Finally, I'm good at something.

224
00:16:27,360 --> 00:16:28,190
Email.

225
00:16:28,320 --> 00:16:29,340
It's from Yoli.

226
00:16:29,900 --> 00:16:31,312
What does she want, Ken?

227
00:16:31,820 --> 00:16:34,761
I don't want to mess up
the dynamics of your team.

228
00:16:34,860 --> 00:16:37,537
Worrying about our team is
the least of our problems.

229
00:16:37,620 --> 00:16:39,120
I say forget about Ken.

230
00:16:39,280 --> 00:16:41,677
We never needed him before,
and we don't need him now.

231
00:16:41,760 --> 00:16:42,857
We can do this on our own.

232
00:16:42,940 --> 00:16:43,770
You're wrong.

233
00:16:43,853 --> 00:16:44,937
Both of you knock it off.

234
00:16:45,020 --> 00:16:46,777
You're acting like a
couple of 12-year-olds.

235
00:16:46,860 --> 00:16:48,095
You know what I mean.

236
00:16:48,760 --> 00:16:49,590
Aquilamon!

237
00:16:49,720 --> 00:16:50,680
You called?

238
00:16:51,040 --> 00:16:53,257
We're going to find
Ken and bring him back.

239
00:16:53,340 --> 00:16:54,811
Hold the fort until then.

240
00:16:55,200 --> 00:16:56,030
Right.

241
00:16:58,140 --> 00:17:00,560
I have created a magnificent specimen.

242
00:17:01,360 --> 00:17:03,040
If I do say so myself.

243
00:17:09,800 --> 00:17:10,630
Ken?

244
00:17:11,200 --> 00:17:13,200
Are you sure you don't want to go?

245
00:17:13,800 --> 00:17:14,660
Go where?

246
00:17:15,100 --> 00:17:16,020
You know where.

247
00:17:16,540 --> 00:17:18,797
Davis and the others
called you, didn't they?

248
00:17:18,880 --> 00:17:21,137
I don't know what you're talking about.

249
00:17:21,220 --> 00:17:22,580
Hey, Ken, it's me!

250
00:17:23,440 --> 00:17:24,270
Huh?

251
00:17:24,353 --> 00:17:25,757
Yoli, what are you doing here?

252
00:17:25,840 --> 00:17:26,877
You have to hurry.

253
00:17:26,960 --> 00:17:29,317
Arukenimon made this
really strong Digimon.

254
00:17:29,400 --> 00:17:30,880
We need Paiildramon.

255
00:17:33,280 --> 00:17:34,110
Ken.

256
00:17:36,200 --> 00:17:37,480
Yoli, I can't go.

257
00:17:38,200 --> 00:17:39,777
You must! I'm sorry.

258
00:17:39,860 --> 00:17:41,380
Why, you...

259
00:17:49,520 --> 00:17:50,960
It's Ken and Yuleen.

260
00:17:51,240 --> 00:17:54,240
I'm sorry I slapped you,
but you needed to wake up.

261
00:18:00,240 --> 00:18:01,416
Let's keep fighting.

262
00:18:01,820 --> 00:18:04,232
I'm sure that Stingmon will show up soon.

263
00:18:05,080 --> 00:18:05,910
Right.

264
00:18:06,680 --> 00:18:07,877
BlackwarGreymon, it's time.

265
00:18:07,960 --> 00:18:10,140
Finish them off once and for all.

266
00:18:13,660 --> 00:18:15,077
Harukenemon is your master.

267
00:18:15,160 --> 00:18:16,984
You must do what she tells you.

